# Convergence orders of composite trapezoid, Simpson and Gauss–Legendre quadrature

**Question.** How fast do three quadrature rules converge, and does the observed order match theory (2, 4, 8)?

## Method

We integrate exp(x), 1/(1+25x²) and √x on [0, 1] (exact values e−1, atan(5)/5, 2/3, in double precision) with the composite trapezoid rule, the composite Simpson rule (one 3-point Simpson application per panel) and composite 4-node Gauss–Legendre (`numpy.polynomial.legendre.leggauss(4)` on each panel), for n = 2^k panels, k = 1…12, and record the absolute error (`results/errors.csv`). For each function and rule we fit log(error) against log(n) by ordinary least squares over the points with error > 10·ε (ε = 2.22·10⁻¹⁶, i.e. error > 2.2·10⁻¹⁵); the order is minus the slope, with a 95 % t‑interval (df = m − 2, m = points used). With fewer than 3 points no interval exists. All numbers come from experiment-repo `results/orders.csv`, `results/fits.json` and `results/README.md` (commit 9a9b92a22be3; code `code/quad.py`).

## Fitted orders

